# Rebuild the Windows exe on commit and push

When the user asks to **commit**, **push**, or **commit and push** this project, rebuild the packaged app so `dist\PDF-Catalog.exe` matches the code being published.

## When

- Do this only for this repo (`pdf-catalog` / PDF-Catalog).
- Do this as part of the same commit/push request, not on every chat message.
- If they commit and push in one request: commit the source, rebuild the exe, then push.
- If they only commit or only push: still rebuild the exe before finishing.

## How

From the repo root, with the project venv:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts\build_exe.py
```

Install PyInstaller into the venv first if the build says it is missing (`pip install pyinstaller`). Wait for the script to finish; it can take several minutes.

## Do not

- Do not commit `dist\`, `build\`, or the exe (they are gitignored).
- Do not skip the rebuild because the change “looks small.”
- Do not treat a failed build as success: report the error and do not claim the exe was updated.
- Do not force-push or skip git hooks to make the rebuild succeed.

Confirm in the reply that `dist\PDF-Catalog.exe` was rebuilt (or that the build failed).
